  "caption": {
    "hashtags": [],
    "public_preview": null,
    "text": "Sometimes the wrong love does not enter your life to ruin you. Sometimes it enters your life to wake you up. To show you where you abandoned yourself trying to be chosen. To show you how much of your peace you were willing to sacrifice just to keep someone from leaving.\n\nAnd that is why healing is so painful at first — because you are not only grieving the person, you are grieving the version of yourself that settled for less than what your heart truly deserved.\n\nBut one day, you will look back at everything that broke you open and realize it was never the end of your story. It was the redirection. The refining. The beginning of finally returning home to yourself.\n\nThe wrong love was never proof that you were hard to love. It was proof that you were always meant for more. \n\n📖Find a copy of this book on Amazon ‘Stay Single’ by Rebecca Simon",
    "word_count": 158
  },
